The project was implemented using Object-Oriented Programming principles in Java.
This project is about a Java console program that lets you have a train ticket booking system.

In this app we can:
-book train tickets
-search train routes
-find direct or indirect train connections
-manage trains and routes as an administrator
-send booking confirmation emails
-send train delay notifications

Features of this application:
-each train has a limited number of seats
-booking is accepted only if there are enough seats available
-failed bookings display an error message
-confirmation emails are shown in the console
-verifies departure and arrival stations
-checks train schedules
-validates changeover times

The administrator of the train station can:
-add train routes
-remove train routes
-modify train routes
-add trains
-remove trains
-modify trains
-view all bookings for a train
-mark trains as delayed
-notify passengers about delays

In Main:
Train stations are made: Brasov, Sinaia, Ploiesti, Bucuresti, Constanta, Cluj.
An additional Timisoara–Cluj route is later added by the administrator.
Several trains are created with predefined schedules and capacities.
The booking functionality is tested using multiple passengers. Marian Cosmin books 2 tickets
and George Paladi books 3 tickets. Another passenger, Marius Moga, attempts to
reserve 200 tickets, but there are only 95 seats available, so an error will occur.
Administrator functionalities are also tested. The administrator displays bookings for a train,
marks a train as delayed by 30 minutes, sends delay notification emails to passengers,
and demonstrates adding and removing routes and trains.